Trochilidae Knowledge Graph (TKG): Biodata Curation
Project Overview
This repository contains the end-to-end computational pipeline for the Trochilidae Knowledge Graph (TKG). The project integrates massive citizen science data (iNaturalist), expert taxonomic authorities (Howard & Moore/HBW), and semantic web technologies (Wikidata/RDF) to generate a high-resolution phenotypic matrix of hummingbird plumage across 14 precise anatomical regions.

Repository Structure
Scripts
scripts/01_data_acquisition.R: Initial harvesting and taxonomic backbone establishment.
scripts/01b_massive_geospatial_thinning.R: Iterative yearly acquisition (2020-2026) and 10 km2 grid-based spatial thinning.
scripts/02_matrix_expansion.R: Generation of the comprehensive 14-region phenotypic matrix (47,320 data points).
scripts/03_semantic_color_dictionary.R: Integration of the HBW/BirdLife color standards with Wikidata.
scripts/04_tkg_interactive_curator.R: Expert-in-the-loop tool for real-time validation of phenotypic traits against in vivo records.
scripts/05_Fig3AandB_geospatial_visualization_and_Barchart.R: Generation of Figure 3 (Hybrid Relief Map & Taxonomic Richness).
scripts/wikidata_biocentric_color_lexicon.sparql: Specialized SPARQL lexicon for semantic Wikification.

Data
data/massive_thinned_observations.csv: The bias-corrected analytical dataset (Big Data scale).
data/color_dictionary_hbw_wikidata.csv: The curated 641-color master list.
data/TKG_Evidence_Annotation_N-Obs.csv: Curated phenotypic assertions with evidence links.
data/tkg_hummingbirds_research_grade.csv: Validated research-grade occurrences.
data/Wikidata_colors.csv: Raw Wikidata color entities before biocentric sanitization.

Key Methodology: Spatial & Taxonomic Integrity
To ensure FAIR principles and scientific rigor, the TKG implements:
Spatial Thinning: Mitigation of the "smartphone proximity effect" via a 0.03 degree resolution grid to ensure biodiversity hotspots reflect biological presence.

14-Region Anatomy: Detailed curation of: Gorget, Crest, Nape, Crown, Bill, Breast, Flanks, Rectrices, Rump, Remiges, Chin, Belly, Tail Coverts, and Back.
LOD Integration: Mapping of all phenotypic traits to unique Wikidata QIDs for machine-readable interoperability.

Getting Started
Clone the repository.

Run scripts/01_data_acquisition.R to establish the core taxa.
Run scripts/01b_massive_geospatial_thinning.R to generate the analytical geospatial dataset.
Execute scripts/04_tkg_interactive_curator.R for the expert validation phase.
Generate final visualizations with scripts/05_Fig3AandB_geospatial_visualization_and_Barchart.R.

